@Lance Dela Cruz  @Lance Dela Cruz  this is a bad argument. I don't think anyone here would ever say you should buy a console for video/photo editing and rendering. Consoles are entertainment machines. If we're looking at it as a gaming/streaming rig, consoles are going to be cheaper every time. The console is 500. The online play subscription is 60 for 1 year. Assuming a console gen lasts 6-9 years, you have paid 540 at most for online subs for 1 year. Your total console cost comes out to 1040, over the course of 9 years. Could you build a pc for a similar price and get the same performance? Maybe, but you're also spending that 1040 up front instead of over time.

If you need to do video rendering/editing, you would never spend 1040 on a pc, you'd be looking at at least 2-3k. Could that pc play games better? Sure. But that pc is also a different use case.

In this conversation the small percentage of video editors aren't being disregarded, they're just not relevant because we're not talking about video editing, we're talking about gaming.

